    <bpmn:process id="W_W3415" name="W3415. Long-Term Supply Agreement &amp; Volume Commitment Negotiation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Strategic-vendor relationship; commodity stabilization; capacity-security need
Frequency: Periodic (1–3 yr agreements)
Volume: Top ~20–50 strategic vendors
Owner: Procurement Director
Participants: Procurement Director, Category Managers, VP Merchandising, Legal (links to VS-100.3), Finance, Vendor
Source: workflow W3415 — Long-Term Supply Agreement &amp; Volume Commitment Negotiation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3415_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3415_Lane1" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3415_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3415_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3415_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3415_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3415_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3415_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3415_Start4" name="Strategic-vendor relationship; commodity stabilization; capacity-security need">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3415_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3415_Task5" name="Category Managers/Procurement build the LTSA business case: commodity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Category Managers/Procurement build the LTSA business case: commodity stability, capacity/alloc security (esp. for steel/cement during construction booms or post-disaster links to VS-69), volume-commitment economics, price/formula terms (links to W3411), and duration; align to the merchandise plan (links to VS-101) and category strategy (links to VS-01)
Responsible (R): Category Managers / Procurement / Finance
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Per agreement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3415_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3415_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3415_Task6" name="Procurement/Legal negotiate and execute the LTSA: volume…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Procurement/Legal negotiate and execute the LTSA: volume commitment/take-or-pay, price/formula (links to W3411), index/cap/floor, termination, force-majeure, quality/SLA, and exclusivity; ensure enforceability and risk allocation (links to VS-100.3/W230)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Legal
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Per agreement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3415_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3415_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3415_Task7" name="Procurement/Finance administer the LTSA: track volume vs commitment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Procurement/Finance administer the LTSA: track volume vs commitment, compliance, pricing, renewal/cancellation, and performance (links to VS-67); report LTSA portfolio and risk to governance (W3406) and the category review (links to VS-01)
Responsible (R): Procurement / Finance
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3415_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3415_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3415_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3415_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3415_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-548 (ensure controlled execution — Procurement Hedging, Forward Buying &amp; Indexed-Pricing Strategy (PA-106.2).) | - operational: flexibility clauses and demand-planning accuracy (links to VS-02); operational: formula/floor design and periodic market-test
Owner: Procurement Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
